-- title:
--   Well-Kindedness of Signature Encoding (Theorem 7), Pattern/Spine Elaboration (Theorems 8 & 9), and Rigid Variable Polarity Classification (Lemmas 3–5)
-- statement:
--   Theorems 7, 8, 9 and Lemmas 3, 4, 5 (Sections 6.1–6.2, pp. 42–47): (1) well-kindedness of polarized signature encoding `EncodeType`; (2) negative-`μ` / positive-`ν` polarity separation of fresh size variables generated by `EncodeType` at `π* = −, π = +`; (3–4) well-typedness of `InferPat` and `InferSpine` in System `F_ω^{cop, SCT}`; and (5–6) four-way polarity classification of rigid size variables in patterns (`PatRigidVarClass`) and copattern spines (`SpineRigidVarClass`).
--
--   **Superseded.** This is the first formalization of Theorems 7–9 and Lemmas 3–5
--   (pp. 43–47) of the thesis. It is refuted through its Lemma 5 conjunct by the
--   accepted disproof `cc630262-14b8-44ff-8ad5-2a36e3725105`. Take
--   $\Psi_1 = [i < \infty]$, $M = \mu^i\langle\rangle$ and $A_0 = M \to (M \to 1)$,
--   and match the first argument with a variable pattern $x$. The index $i$ then
--   occurs positively in the type of $x$ and negatively in the remaining type
--   $M \to 1$, so none of the four mutually exclusive classes of Lemma 5 applies. A
--   separate checked result shows that the thesis's signature encoding never
--   produces a type in which one inductive index occurs in two argument positions
--   like this, so the counterexample exploits an input more general than the thesis
--   considers. The Theorem 7, Lemma 3 and Theorems 8–9 conjuncts are not refuted.
--   Corrected statement: `NishtAbel2024V2.theorems_7_8_9_and_lemmas_3_4_5`. It
--   restates Lemmas 4–5 as polarity bounds on kinding-aware occurrences (`CheckUse`)
--   instead of the four-way classification.
-- source:
--   Kanstantsin Nisht, 'Type-Based Termination Checking in Agda', Master's Thesis in Computer Science and Engineering, Chalmers University of Technology and University of Gothenburg (supervised by Andreas Abel), 2024; extended abstract by Kanstantsin Nisht and Andreas Abel, 30th International Conference on Types for Proofs and Programs (TYPES 2024). Sections 6.1–6.2, Theorem 7 (p. 43), Lemma 3 (p. 43), Theorem 8 (p. 45), Theorem 9 (p. 45), Lemma 4 (pp. 45–46), and Lemma 5 (pp. 46–47).

import Definitions.Def_NishtAbel2024_Syntax
import Definitions.Def_NishtAbel2024_Inference

namespace NishtAbel2024

/-- Theorem 7 (p. 43), Lemma 3 (p. 43), Theorem 8 (p. 45), Theorem 9 (p. 45),
Lemma 4 (pp. 45–46), and Lemma 5 (pp. 46–47):
1. (**Theorem 7**) If `π; Δ ⊢_{SCT}^{π*} A ⇒ Ψ; A'` for `Δ ⊢_{F_ω} A ⇐ *`, then `Δ ⊢ ∀Ψ. A' ⇐ *`.
2. (**Lemma 3**) If `+; Δ ⊢_{SCT}^− A ⇒ Ψ; A'`, then every `i ∈ Ψ` either occurs negatively as a
   `μ`-size variable in `A'` or positively as a `ν`-size variable in `A'` (exclusively).
3. (**Theorem 8**) If `Δ₀ ⊢_{SCT} p : A ⇒ Γ; Δ; Ψ; p'`, then `Δ; Γ ⊢_{Δ₀} p' ⇐ A`.
4. (**Theorem 9**) If `Δ₀ ⊢_{SCT} q⃗ : A ⇒ C; Γ; Δ; Ψ; q⃗'`, then `Δ; Γ | A ⊢_{Δ₀} q⃗' ⇒ C`.
5. (**Lemma 4**) Under `PositiveFixpointHygiene Δ₀ A₀`, if `Δ₀ ⊢_{SCT} p : A₀ ⇒ Γ; Δ; Ψ; p'`,
   then every `i ∈ Ψ` satisfies `PatRigidVarClass`.
6. (**Lemma 5**) Under `SignatureFixpointHygiene`, if
   `Δ₀, Ψ₁ ⊢_{SCT} q⃗ : A₀ ⇒ A''; Γ; Δ; Ψ₂; q⃗'`, then every `i ∈ Ψ₁ ++ Ψ₂` satisfies
   `SpineRigidVarClass`. -/
theorem theorems_7_8_9_and_lemmas_3_4_5 :
    (∀ (πstar π : Polarity) (Δ : KindingCtx) (A A' : TypeExpr) (Ψ : SizeCtx),
      SizeCtxWf Δ.sizes →
      FwKindCheck Δ A .star →
      EncodeType πstar π Δ A Ψ A' →
      KindCheck Δ (TypeExpr.forallSizes Ψ A') .star) ∧
    (∀ (Δ : KindingCtx) (A A' : TypeExpr) (Ψ : SizeCtx),
      EncodeType .neg .pos Δ A Ψ A' →
      ∀ i ∈ Ψ.dom,
        (SizeOccursFixPol (Δ.extSizes Ψ) .mu i .neg A' ∧
          ¬ SizeOccursFixPol (Δ.extSizes Ψ) .nu i .pos A') ∨
        (SizeOccursFixPol (Δ.extSizes Ψ) .nu i .pos A' ∧
          ¬ SizeOccursFixPol (Δ.extSizes Ψ) .mu i .neg A')) ∧
    (∀ (Δ₀ : KindingCtx) (p p' : Pat) (A : TypeExpr)
       (Γ : TermCtx) (Δ : List TyDecl) (Ψ : SizeCtx),
      InferPat Δ₀ p A Γ Δ Ψ p' →
      PatTyping Δ₀ Δ Γ p' A) ∧
    (∀ (Δ₀ : KindingCtx) (qs qs' : PatSpine) (A C : TypeExpr)
       (Γ : TermCtx) (Δ : List TyDecl) (Ψ : SizeCtx),
      InferSpine Δ₀ qs A C Γ Δ Ψ qs' →
      SpineTyping Δ₀ Δ Γ A qs' C) ∧
    (∀ (Δ₀ : KindingCtx) (p p' : Pat) (A₀ : TypeExpr)
       (Γ : TermCtx) (Δ : List TyDecl) (Ψ : SizeCtx),
      PositiveFixpointHygiene Δ₀ A₀ →
      InferPat Δ₀ p A₀ Γ Δ Ψ p' →
      ∀ i ∈ Ψ.dom, PatRigidVarClass (Δ₀.append ⟨Ψ, Δ⟩) Γ i) ∧
    (∀ (Δ₀ : KindingCtx) (Ψ₁ Ψ₂ : SizeCtx) (qs qs' : PatSpine)
       (A₀ A'' : TypeExpr) (Γ : TermCtx) (Δ : List TyDecl),
      SignatureFixpointHygiene (Δ₀.extSizes Ψ₁) A₀ →
      InferSpine (Δ₀.extSizes Ψ₁) qs A₀ A'' Γ Δ Ψ₂ qs' →
      ∀ i ∈ (Ψ₁ ++ Ψ₂).dom,
        SpineRigidVarClass ((Δ₀.extSizes Ψ₁).append ⟨Ψ₂, Δ⟩) Γ A'' i) := by
  sorry

end NishtAbel2024
